-- title:
--   A whole rational row (including its constant coordinate) can be cleared at once.
-- statement:
--   A whole rational row (including its constant coordinate) can be cleared at
--   once. Neither bound depends on how many other rows the system has.
--
--   This lemma is part of OpenAI's machine-checked proof that rational linear programs can be solved by a strongly polynomial algorithm on a real-number RAM (Smale's ninth problem). It is used in the proof of `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.Compression.exists_integer_projection_system`, `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.Compression.exists_small_rat_of_tight_system`.
